------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0. WHAT THIS SURFACE IS (parity analysis)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web source is a HEADLESS, side-effect-only component: `export function
FormatterPrefsBridge(): null`. It renders nothing. It:
  1. Keeps a permanent subscriber to the ['settings'] query so cross-tab
     invalidations always refetch.
  2. On resolved settings, applies resolveLocale(settings.locale) +
     (settings.decimal_precision ?? 2) to the module-level numberFormat globals
     (_globalLocale / _globalPrecision), deduped vs the last value AND the
     current global (lastLocale/lastDecimals refs + getGlobal* guards).
  3. Subscribes to the TOPICS.SETTINGS_CHANGED broadcast and forces a refetch
     (queryClient.invalidateQueries(['settings'])) as defense-in-depth.

It extracts NO t() calls (anonymous surface — confirmed by the prompt's i18n
inventory: "none"). No charts, no maps, no shared components.

The native parity reproduces this DATA + BEHAVIOR (not invented visual chrome):
a faithful headless SwiftUI bridge, fully Shared-free and design-token-free
(ADR-002/ADR-005), so it host-compiles and host-tests in isolation.

Data-source seam mapping (web -> native, P1/S8):
  useSettings / useSettingsQuery -> FormatterPrefsSettingsProvider (no HTTP in view)
  useQueryClient.invalidateQueries(['settings']) -> provider.refresh()
  subscribe(TOPICS.SETTINGS_CHANGED) -> FormatterPrefsChangeSignal (NotificationCenter)
  numberFormat _globalLocale/_globalPrecision -> FormatterPreferences (the holder)
  resolveLocale (locale.ts) -> FormatterPrefsAdapter.resolveLocale
  fmtNumber/fmtInt/fmtPercent/fmtWithUnit -> FormatterPreferences facade

States (every web settings-query state, reproduced behaviorally + tested):
  loading | empty | error(failed) | stale(freshness) | offline(freshness)

P1/S11 diagnostics: emits `view.opened` with slug "FormatterPrefsBridge" on
appear (OSLog sink, redaction-safe, no PII).

Files shipped (apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/):
  FormatterPrefsBridge.swift            headless View + onAppear view.opened
  FormatterPrefsBridge.Model.swift      state/freshness enums, provider+signal+
                                        telemetry seams, @Observable model
  FormatterPrefsBridge.Globals.swift    FormatterPreferences holder + adapter
  FormatterPrefsBridge.Providers.swift  system provider + NotificationCenter
                                        signal + in-memory doubles
  FormatterPrefsBridge.Previews.swift   pure inspector model + DEBUG inspector +
                                        per-state #Preview
  FormatterPrefsBridge.Tests.swift      XCTest (35 tests)
  FormatterPrefsBridge.strings          i18n table (anonymous surface; documented,
                                        zero parity keys — surface has no user copy)

